  "solution": {
    "text": "The reaction of an ester (other than format) with Grignard&rsquo;s reagent followed by hydrolysis in acidic medium produces a tertiary alcohol.\r\n\r\n<img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_advanced/35_solu_chem_par_2.jpg\" style=\"width: 772px; height: 312px;\" />\r\n\r\nThe dehydration of <math> <mrow> <msup> <mn>3</mn> <mn>o</mn>&#160;</msup></mrow></math>-alcohol at <math> <mrow> <msup> <mtext>O</mtext> <mtext>o</mtext> </msup> <mtext>C</mtext></mrow> </math> in the given compound produces an alkyl group in the benzene ring. This compound on reaction with <math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>COCl</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> in <math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>CH</mtext></mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>Cl</mtext></mrow> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> </mrow> </math> and shows Friedel craft&#39;s alkylation reaction",
